Getting SX Going Quickly:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1)	Install it!

2)	Check conferences and filepaths for each. The config comes with
	these, so change them to your likeing:

	1. New Users   files:new/
	2. BBS         files:bbs/
	3. Warez			files:warez/
	4. Request		files:req/

	(these paths should be used to store files on hdd)

	To change these paths run SX-Config and click on the "Conf/Msg/File"
	button. You might want to edit SX:Confs/<conf>/paths also.

3)	Load SX-Config and click on "This Node", and change the
	"FileCheckDir". This should be a empty directory for the BBS
	to do some work in, you must create it! You should do this for
	every node.

4)	Type in shell "SX:Utils/SAmiLog -C"
	This will create a storage file, so that the last callers program
	can work.

5)	run SX:SX-MCP

6)	run a node! eg: "run sx:sx 1" will load node 1


Graphics Card Users:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	You must:

	1) Load SX-Config
	2) Select "Local Display"
	3) Choose a valid screen mode that your gfxcard can handle
	4) Go back to the main SX-Config window
	5) Choose "Display Modes"
	6) Change the screenmode for each display mode, ansi/ascii etc

	To make this take effect for every node, you can do something like

	copy sx:node1/prefs/LocalDis.DAT sx:node2/prefs/

	etc etc...
